refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns the contents of the current session encoded, &return.falseforfailure;.
&false; is returned, with an E_WARNING, when $_SESSION is not an array, or when the php handler finds a key containing |.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     An E_WARNING is now emitted, instead of silently
     returning &false;, when a key contains | with the
     php handler.




    8.0.0

     The diagnostic for a skipped integer key is now an
     E_WARNING instead of an E_NOTICE.

&reftitle.notes;
$_SESSION must be an array, which is normally set up by session_start.
With the php and php_binary handlers, integer keys are skipped, with an E_WARNING. The php_binary handler also silently skips keys longer than 127 bytes.
